    keywords: 'hourly by the hour per hour rate hours a week retainer monthly virtual assistant freelancer timesheet log hours weekly pay hire',
    summary: 'A hirer pays someone by the hour or monthly: for example a virtual assistant at 15 USDC an hour, up to 20 hours a week, for 4 weeks. There are two ways in: name someone they know by Karwan tag (Start a trade, Hire by the hour, at /work/new, or propose_hourly_work), or post the work on the market (/work/requests/new, or propose_post_hourly_work) with the most per hour, hours a week and how long; posting moves no money. Sellers who fit are told and offer a rate with a note (propose_hourly_offer; offering again changes it). A seller who saved an hourly or monthly way (set_way_i_deal with hourly or monthly) has their agent offer at once when fitting work is posted: the usual rate lowered to the hirer\'s most, never under their lowest, and only when the hours fit; they are told and can change or withdraw it. The hirer\'s agent ranks the offers by what each person has actually done on Karwan: skill fit from what they sell and have done first, verified above unverified, then rating, then the lower rate; nobody uploads samples. The hirer sees up to five, the best fit recommended, each with name and tag, verified in words, tier, rating and up to three reasons, never scores or counts (read_hourly_request). Hiring one (propose_hire_offer) pays for the first week and the worker\'s agent accepts the terms they offered at once. Offers close a day before the start; with nobody hired the work closes. The card shows the first week, the Karwan fee (half of 1 percent), what the hirer pays now and the most for the whole engagement. The hirer pays one week (or month) at a time, held on the escrow until it settles; a worker new to Karwan is paid one week at a time, and after they finish work on Karwan the hirer can pay up to 4 weeks ahead. The worker accepts before it starts, or the money comes back by itself. The worker logs hours by the minute from the week starting until 2 days after it ends (propose_hours); hours go to the week running now unless they name an earlier one still open. The hirer then has 3 days to approve (paid at once) or say how many hours are wrong and why (propose_hours_object, only after logging closes); silence pays when review ends, and unused budget goes back every week. Objected hours wait 72 hours for both sides, then go to Karwan\'s review team; if they do not rule in 5 days the hours are split half and half, and the rest of the week is paid at once. Either side ends with one week\'s notice (one month for a retainer). A finished engagement goes on both records. In Telegram, offering, paying for a week, approving or objecting and taking back an offer open Karwan to confirm; accepting, logging hours and notice stay in the chat. Arc Testnet only, up to about 1,000 USDC held at once for now.',
