    id: 'delivery', title: 'Delivery, review and payment release', status: 'testnet', mainnet: 'off', route: '/deals/[id]',
    pages: ['/deals', '/deals/[id]', '/cashout/[jobId]'],
    api: ['POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/delivered', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/release', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/claim', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/extension/request', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/extension/respond', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/arrived', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/handover-code', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/evidence/manual-review', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/still-reviewing', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/delay-appeal', 'POST /api/deals/direct/:jobId/delay-appeal-respond'],
    tools: ['propose_mark_delivered', 'propose_release', 'get_deal_status', 'propose_extension', 'propose_confirm_goods_received', 'message_in_deal', 'propose_recheck_payout', 'propose_goods_arrived', 'propose_review_delivery_myself', 'propose_claim_payment', 'propose_more_review_time', 'propose_delay_appeal', 'show_handover_code'],
    keywords: 'my deals deals list needs you finished deals deliver delivery mark delivered review release pay milestone approve work done tracking carrier proceeds flagged unsafe link blocked wrongly flagged safe link support check held match match held for a look security agent screen',
    summary: 'Every deal is in Deals (/deals): what needs you first, then active ones, then finished ones; Home shows the top of that list, and on a phone Deals is the third tab. The deal page opens with who the deal is with, its reference, where the money is, the amount, one line for now and the one move; below it, rows open in place: Progress (with the latest activity), Delivery, Handover code, Get paid now, Agreement, Receipts, and Something is wrong, with anything that needs the person at the top. Messages open beside the deal from the message button next to the name of the other side. Point people to the row by that name. The seller marks each milestone delivered with a link. Karwan checks every delivered link for safety and against the agreed request; a delivery that may not match pauses the payment while the money stays held, and the seller can send the right link. When the safety check flags a link, the buyer cannot open it and the seller sees two buttons on the deal: Send a new delivery link, and My link is safe. Ask a person to check, which opens a support chat with the deal attached. A person at Karwan opens the link safely and either clears it (the buyer can then open it, marked Checked by Karwan support, the seller\'s record is not marked down for it, and payment follows the usual steps) or keeps it blocked, and the seller is told to send a new link. While a link is held nothing is paid for it, not even when the review time of the buyer ends; this holds on every escrow, the new family included. A link the check rated malicious needs both a support reviewer and an administrator at Karwan to clear it. A new delivery is checked again from the start. A passed check does not guarantee quality. The buyer reviews within the window in the terms and releases payment. On deals held by the new escrow each milestone is delivered on its own: once a milestone is paid, the seller delivers the next one, and only then can the buyer release it or does its review time start. If more time is needed, the seller can ask for more time to deliver (propose_extension) and the buyer can extend the review window, up to the limit in the terms. Karwan reminds the seller a day before the delivery date (halfway when the whole delivery time is under two days). When the date passes with nothing delivered, both sides are told: the seller has the grace period, one day, to deliver, then the buyer\'s money goes back to them automatically. The seller can ask for more time any number of times before the date, one request at a time, and once more after it while the grace runs. A request the buyer has not answered holds that refund: the money stays in the deal until the buyer approves or declines, and Karwan reminds the buyer up to three times, a day apart. A decline lets the refund go ahead; an approval adds the days to the later of the old date and the moment of approval. When the review time ends with no release and no problem raised, the payment goes to the seller, the final one included: on deals held by the new escrow Karwan sends it, and on deals held by the earlier escrow the seller claims it. Proceeds go to the seller agent. Every one of these steps can be asked of the assistant, which shows one card and runs the deal page\'s own step: the buyer says the goods arrived (it starts their review time and pays nothing), reviews a delivery themselves when the delivery check has not answered, or adds review time while still checking; the seller claims a payment the buyer left in silence on a deal held by the earlier escrow, or asks a buyer who is sitting on a release to release it, and the buyer answers with a reason that keeps the payment held. With no answer in time the payment goes to the seller. In Telegram, claiming a payment opens the deal page, where it is confirmed. On a goods deal the buyer can also confirm on the trade record that the goods reached them, which does not pay the seller; Karwan signs it for wallets it holds, and someone with their own wallet signs it on the deal page. Either side can write in the deal chat through the assistant (message_in_deal); a message never moves money or changes the deal. If a released payment did not confirm, the deal shows it needs attention and the buyer can have it checked again (propose_recheck_payout); nothing is paid twice. Separately from links, the security agent screens each match when it is funded. A match it holds shows Held for a look on the deal, with one shared line and only the lines meant for that side; the money stays in escrow and release follows the deal\u2019s own rules, nothing is blocked. Either person can ask a person at Karwan to check from that card, and a person at Karwan clears the hold with a reason; both then see one line in the deal chat. A person at Karwan can also review an earlier delivery link, or one on a closed deal, for the record: clearing it takes the offence off the seller and changes nothing for the money.',
    steps: ['Seller: open the deal and mark the milestone delivered with the evidence.', 'What a delivery carries depends on the kind of deal: work is a link to it; goods sent by a courier are the carrier and tracking number (DHL, FedEx, UPS, the shipping lines, and GIG Logistics, Kwik, NIPOST, Aramex, Emirates Post, Delhivery, India Post, Bosta with the courier’s tracking page link); goods handed over in person end with the buyer’s six-digit handover code. Goods over 50 USDC also need a photo of the item. Up to four photos go with any delivery, from the deliver form or sent to the assistant with a caption like delivered or packed.', 'Handover in person: the buyer shows their code (Show my handover code on the deal, or show_handover_code) only once they hold the item; the seller enters it when delivering. It works once, counts as the item arriving and starts the buyer’s review; five wrong tries lock it for 15 minutes; asking again makes a new code.', 'Both sides see the Delivery card on the deal page: each link in the seller’s note as its own Open button, the carrier, tracking number with Track shipment and Copy, the date sent and arrived, what Karwan checked (links point to real sites, the tracking number fits the carrier, and for the buyer only whether it matches the request), documents, and earlier deliveries per milestone. The buyer confirms goods arrived there with It arrived, which starts their review and does not pay the seller. The assistant answers where is my order and what did they deliver from get_deal_status.', 'Buyer: review and release, or ask for an extension or open a dispute.', 'Seller: withdraw proceeds from /cashout/[jobId] or the seller agent.'],
